<title>USA: Pittsburgh baseball fans asked to back new stadium.</title>
<headline>Pittsburgh baseball fans asked to back new stadium.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pittsburgh Pirates are asking fans to support a November referendum calling for a 1/2 percent sales tax increase in 10 counties around Pittsburgh, the Pittsburgh Post Gazette reported.</p>
<p>Pirates team owner Kevin McClatchy sent a letter to the team's 4,000 season ticket owners urging their support for the increase, which would help fund a new baseball-only stadium for the Pirates.</p>
<p>Many of the affected counties have already said they would not support a tax increase.</p>
<p>The National League baseball team has gotten off to a better start this season than many had expected.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
